  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Alleviating The Impact Of The Ukraine Crisis On Yemen Through The Provision Of Provision Of Life-Saving Multi-Sectoral Assistance To Food Insecure Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the escalation of conflict in March 2015, the humanitarian situation in Yemen has led to unprecedented suffering across the country.  Trends point to a deteriorating humanitarian and food security situation in Yemen, with fighting and clashes exacerbating existing vulnerabilities, stalled development gains made in the years preceding, and has driven the country to the brink of famine.  The conflict in Ukraine is contributing to even further deteriorating conditions in Yemen, and experts predict that Yemen will continue to grapple with the ripple effects of the recent hikes in the price of petroleum and diesel and project that direct and indirect ramifications of the Russia-Ukraine war on the prices of minimum food baskets would be devastating. In line with Yemen&#x2019;s Humanitarian Response Plan for 2022 and IOM&#x2019;s Crisis Response Plan for Yemen, IOM proposes to contribute towards alleviating the immediate suffering of food insecure populations with timely and high-impact multi-sectoral (Health, water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH), Protection, and multi-purpose cash) interventions, as well as complementary interventions such as assessments through IOM&#x2019;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) that are crucial for informing the integrated response.</narrative>
  </description>
